fmt writes through os.Stdout, which is a nil @File on bare-metal by design
(os_baremetal.bn: "a bare-metal target has no standard output" — its Write
returns errNoFS), so fmt.Print produces no output there and the expected text is
unattainable — the program prints nothing and the test "fails" with empty
output.  This is the same environment limitation the other fmt tests
(1090_fmt_basic etc.) are xfailed for, not a codegen bug: the const-fold this
test actually exercises is backend-independent and verified on every hosted / VM
mode (and would work on baremetal via testing.Println, which reaches the console
through semihosting).  One marker covers BOTH baremetal lanes:
builder-comp_arm32_baremetal (this file, LLVM) and
builder-comp_native_arm32_baremetal (via OVERRIDE_MODE in run.sh).
